WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.385
Lesson 11.1.

00:00:02.385 --> 00:00:05.330
Hedging price exposure with perps and options.

00:00:05.330 --> 00:00:07.226
By the end of this lesson, you'll

00:00:07.226 --> 00:00:09.846
be able to reduce price exposure deliberately,

00:00:09.846 --> 00:00:11.575
and know what each hedge costs.

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:14.165
Here's the plan.

00:00:14.165 --> 00:00:15.850
First, the key ideas.

00:00:15.850 --> 00:00:18.565
Then, a worked example, step by step.

00:00:18.565 --> 00:00:20.090
Then, your checklist.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.252
And finally, a three-question quiz.

00:00:23.552 --> 00:00:26.059
pays or earns funding; needs margin;

00:00:26.059 --> 00:00:28.460
the hedge ratio is your choice.

00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:30.716
First, Perp hedge: short a perpetual

00:00:30.716 --> 00:00:32.785
future against spot you hold.

00:00:32.785 --> 00:00:34.115
Cheap to open;.

00:00:34.115 --> 00:00:36.169
Next, Protective put: buy the right

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.610
to sell at a strike.

00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:39.299
Costs a premium, and your loss

00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:41.070
is capped below the strike.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.035
Then, Collar: buy a put and sell

00:00:43.035 --> 00:00:44.585
a call to pay for it.

00:00:44.585 --> 00:00:47.815
Cheaper protection in exchange for capped upside.

00:00:47.815 --> 00:00:49.365
And finally, A hedge costs

00:00:49.365 --> 00:00:52.190
something (premium, funding, capped upside).

00:00:52.190 --> 00:00:54.865
Hedge the risk you can't afford, not every risk.

00:00:56.165 --> 00:00:58.680
Let's work an example, step by step.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:03.305
You hold 10 ETH at $3,000 ($30,000).

00:01:03.305 --> 00:01:08.590
50% perp hedge (short 5 ETH): ETH falls

00:01:08.590 --> 00:01:14.272
30% to spot minus $9,000, short +$4,500 to

00:01:14.272 --> 00:01:20.650
minus $4,500 (minus 15%) instead of minus 30%.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:24.166
Protective put: buy a 30-day

00:01:24.166 --> 00:01:27.860
$2,700 put for 2% ($60/ETH).

00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:31.728
Worst case per ETH = $300 drop to

00:01:31.728 --> 00:01:36.165
the strike + $60 premium = $360 (12%),

00:01:36.165 --> 00:01:40.260
however far ETH falls in that month.

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:43.020
Here's your checklist.

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:44.555
Do it now, for real.

00:01:44.555 --> 00:01:47.860
First, Hedge target stated (which risk, how much).

00:01:47.860 --> 00:01:51.455
Next, Cost computed (premium, funding, capped upside).

00:01:51.455 --> 00:01:54.515
And finally, Margin buffer for perp hedges set.

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:57.025
Question 1.

00:01:57.025 --> 00:01:58.600
What does a protective put cap?

00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:05.681
The answer: Your loss below the strike, for the

00:02:05.681 --> 00:02:08.010
option's term, at the cost of the premium.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.555
Question 2.

00:02:10.555 --> 00:02:12.010
What does a collar trade away?

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.328
The answer: Upside above the call

00:02:18.328 --> 00:02:19.835
strike, to pay for the put.

00:02:21.135 --> 00:02:22.405
Question 3.

00:02:22.405 --> 00:02:27.355
20 ETH, 25% perp hedge, ETH −40%.

00:02:27.355 --> 00:02:30.090
Net loss if ETH was $3,000?

00:02:34.510 --> 00:02:42.165
The answer: Spot −$24,000, short +$6,000 → −$18,000.

00:02:43.465 --> 00:02:44.710
Let's recap.

00:02:44.710 --> 00:02:46.454
Perp hedge: short a perpetual

00:02:46.454 --> 00:02:48.440
future against spot you hold.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:50.117
Protective put: buy the right

00:02:50.117 --> 00:02:51.535
to sell at a strike.

00:02:51.535 --> 00:02:53.026
Collar: buy a put and sell

00:02:53.026 --> 00:02:54.485
a call to pay for it.

00:02:54.485 --> 00:02:57.825
A hedge costs something (premium, funding, capped upside).

00:02:59.125 --> 00:03:01.640
Do the checklist now, before you move on.

00:03:01.640 --> 00:03:06.725
Next up, Lesson 11.2: Depeg, protocol and smart-contract cover.
